bian Fett, Apple (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/fabianfett","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ian Partridge, IBM (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/ianpartridge"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Jimmy McDermott, Transeo (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/jdmcd"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Johannes Weiss, Apple ("},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/weissi","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Kaitlin Mahar, MongoDB ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/kmahar","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Logan Wright, Vapor ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/loganwright"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Patrick Freed, MongoDB ("},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/patrickfreed","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Paulo Faria, Zewo ("},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/paulofaria","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Steve Algernon, Apple ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/salgernon"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tanner Nelson, Vapor"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Todd Varland, Amazon ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/toddvarland"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tom Doron, Apple, Core team rep (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/tomerd","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Communication","text":"Communication"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Swift Server workgroup uses the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/forums.swift.org\/c\/server","isActive":true},{"text":" for general discussion.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Community Participation","level":2,"anchor":"Community-Participation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Everyone is welcome to contribute in the following ways:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Proposing new libraries and tools to be considered."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Participating in design discussions.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Asking or answering questions on the forums.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reporting or triaging bugs."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Submitting pull requests to the library projects for implementation or tests.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"These conversations will take place on the "},{"overridingTitle":"Swift Server forum","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift Server forum"}],"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/forums.swift.org\/c\/server"},{"type":"text","text":". Over time, the workgroup may form smaller working groups to focus on specific technology areas."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Charter","text":"Charter"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The main goal of the Swift Server workgroup is to eventually recommend libraries and tools for server application development with Swift. The difference between this workgroup and the Swift Evolution process is that server-oriented libraries and tools that are produced as a result of workgroup efforts will exist outside of the Swift language project itself. The workgroup will work to nurture, mature and recommend projects as they move into their development and release stages."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Membership","text":"Membership","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Membership in the workgroup is contribution-based and expected to evolve over time. Adding new members and removing inactive ones is subject to a SSWG vote and requires unanimous agreement. A cap of two members per company is in place to avoid overweight representation. A cap of ten members total is in place to keep the group small enough to be effective. Membership term is capped at 2 years, but exiting members may re-apply at the end of their term. When multiple candidates compete for the same seat, the SSWG will vote between all candidates, with a final voting round between the two candidates that received most votes in the first round."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Companies or individuals that would like to join the workgroup should apply by posting a request to the "},{"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift Server forum"}],"overridingTitle":"Swift Server forum","type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/forums.swift.org\/c\/server","isActive":true},{"text":". Applicants will then be invited to the next available SSWG meeting to present their case.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inactive members that do not participate in four consecutive workgroup meetings will be contacted to confirm their desire to stay with the group. After missing ten consecutive meetings, the SSWG will vote on removing them from the group."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Voting","type":"heading","text":"Voting"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In various situations the SSWG shall hold a vote. These votes can happen on the phone, email, or via a voting service, when appropriate. SSWG members can either respond “agree, yes, +1”, “disagree, no, -1”, or “abstain”. A vote passes with two-thirds vote of votes cast based on the SSWG charter. An abstain vote equals not voting at all.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Meeting-Time","text":"Meeting Time","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The SSWG meets biweekly on Wednesday at 2:00PM PT (USA Pacific). The meetings take place in the weeks with the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"http:\/\/www.whatweekisit.org","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations","doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations\/swift-groups"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift Server workgroup is a steering team that promotes the use of Swift for developing and deploying server applications. The Swift Server workgroup will:"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"https://github.com/weissi":{"type":"link","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/weissi","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/weissi","title":"@weissi","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"@weissi","type":"text"}]},"doc://project-operations/documentation/project-operations/windows-workgroup":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations\/windows-workgroup","url":"\/documentation\/project-operations\/windows-workgroup","title":"Windows Workgroup","role":"ar